# Total an invoice from JSON, skip lines with no quantity, and print each line.
Allow reading files
Also use "pricing.writ"

To TotalDocument, given a document which is a string, returning a decimal
    the data is the document as JSON
    the invoice is the data as an Invoice
    return TotalInvoice with the invoice

To TotalFile, given a path which is a string, returning a decimal
    try to
        the text is the contents of the file at the path
    if that fails
        warn "Could not read {the path}: {the error}"
        return 0
    return TotalDocument with the text

To TotalInvoice, given an invoice which is an Invoice, returning a decimal
    the lines are the lines of the invoice
    the billable are the lines where the quantity is greater than 0
    the subtotal is the sum of price times quantity for each item in the billable
    the rate is TaxRate with the region of the invoice
    the tax is the subtotal times the rate
    the due is the subtotal plus the tax rounded to 2 places
    for each line in the billable
        the amount is LineTotal with the line
        say "{the sku of the line} x {the quantity of the line} = {the amount}"
    say "Due {the due}"
    return the due

When run, given a document which is a string, returning a decimal
    return TotalDocument with the document
